I have rice and dal in my cart.
Now I want coffee.
I like coffee a lot.
I look around.
There are many racks here.
But I do not see coffee anywhere.
I see a worker there.
I go to him.
I call out to him.
"Dada, excuse me," I say.
The worker looks at me.
"Yes, madam," he says.
"Where is the coffee?" I ask.
"I want coffee powder."
"Where are the hot drinks?"
He smiles.
"Hot drinks are in aisle number three," he says.
He points to the right.
"Thank you, Dada," I say.
I go to aisle number three.
